$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Using 3b: To a stirred solution of 1a (30.0 mg, 0.18 mmol), finely
grounded 3b (15.0 mg, 0.018 mmol) and TMAF (1.6 mg, 0.018 mmol) in
toluene/CH2Cl2 (2/1, 0.5 mL) Me3SiCF3 (52.2 μL, 0.35 mmol) was added at
-80°C under N2 atmosphere. After the reaction mixture was stirred for 6 h
at the same temperature, it was quenched with sat. NH4Cl aq. The aqueous
layer was extracted with AcOEt (5 mL x 2), and the combined organic
layers were washed with brine, dried over MgSO4 and concentrated under
reduced pressure to furnish the crude 2a as a trimethylsilyl ether. The
trimethylsilyl ether was treated with TBAF (50.6 mg, 0.19 mmol) in THF
(1.5 mL) at room temperature for 1h. The resulting mixture was
concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel (acetone/n-hexane= 10/1) to give 2a (36.9
mg, 87%, 85% ee) as a white solid
1.1.1-trifluoro-2-(naphthalen-2yl)propan-2-ol (2a), yield (36.9 mg, 87%)
The ee of the product was determined by HPLC using a OD-H column
(n-hexane/i-PrOH = 95/5, flow rate 0.5 mL/min, λ = 254 nm, τmaj =18.1
min, τmin = 28.3 min).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 87% ee
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Cinchona alkaloids/TMAF combination-catalyzed nucleophilic
enantioselective trifluoromethylation of aryl ketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mizuta, Satoshi; Shibata, Norio; Akiti, Surendar; Fujimoto, Hiroyuki;
Nakamura, Shuichi; Toru, Takeshi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2007), 9(18), 3707-3710

