$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Synthesis of Trifluoromethyl Silyl Ethers
(R)-10-12: To a solution of ketoamide 4-6 (1 equiv) and
trifluoromethyl(trimethyl)silane (1.2 equiv) in DMF was added, at rt
under Ar, potassium carbonate (0.05-0.15 equiv). After the complete
conversion of starting ketoamide (reaction monitored by GC), the reaction
was quenched with a saturated aqueous solution of NH4Cl and extracted
thrice with Et2O. The combined organic layers were washed with brine,
dried (MgSO4) and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by chromatography (PE/Et2O) and recrystallised (for solid
compounds).
(–)-(4R,5R)-2,2-Dimethyl-5-((R)-2,2,2-trifluoro-1-phenyl-1-trimethylsilanyloxy-ethyl)-[1,3]dioxolane-4-carboxylic
acid methoxy-methyl-amide (R)-10. According to the general procedure, a
mixture of ketoamide 4 (164 mg, 0.56 mmol), CF3TMS (0.10 mL, 0.68 mmol,
1.2 equiv) and K2CO3 (8 mg, 0.06mmol, 0.10 equiv) in DMF (5 mL) was
stirred for 2h 30. Purification of the residue (mixture of two
diastereomers 94:6) by chromatography (PE/EtOAc 90:10) afforded the major
diastereomer (R)-10 (218 mg, 90%) as a colourless oil. tR = 11.7 min;
[α]D20 -17.2 (c 0.97, CHCl3); 19F NMR (235.3 MHz) δ -75.3 (s, 3F, CF3);
1H NMR (250 MHz): δ 0.18 (s, 9H), 1.34 (s, 3H), 1.47 (s, 3H), 3.24 (s,
3H), 3.67 (s, 3H), 4.71 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H), 5.34 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H),
7.37-7.39 (m, 3H), 7.66 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (62.9 MHz) δ 1.9, 26.0, 26.4,
32.4, 61.9, 72.1, 78.3, 80.1 (q, J = 27.5 Hz), 111.7, 124.8 (q, J = 288.0
Hz, CF3), 127.8, 128.2, 128.9, 135.4, 169.8. HRMS (ESI+): m/z calcd for
C19H28F3NO5SiNa [M+Na]+458.1587, found 458.1577.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 94:6 crude diastereomeric ratio, optimization study,
optimized on initiator, solvent and reaction temp.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantiopure Quaternary α-Trifluoromethyl-α-alkoxyaldehydes from
L-Tartaric Acid Derived Ketoamides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Nonnenmacher, Jean; Massicot, Fabien; Grellepois, Fabienne; Portella,
Charles
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2008), 73(20), 7990-7995

