$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To aldehyde (0.60 g, 4.5 rnmol) in a dry flask under N2 were added DMF
(anhydrous, 5 mL)and TMSCF3 (1.9 g, 13.5 mmol). After the mixture was
cooled to -25 °C, carbene 1 (7mg, 0.021 rnmol, 0.005 eq) was added. The
mixture was warmed to room temperatureand stirred at that temperature
until aldehyde was consumed as determined by HPLC (60 min).A 2 N HCl
solution (6 mL) was added and the solution was stirred at room
temperatureuntil all TMS protected intermediate converted to product.
Water (30 mL) was added andthe aqueous layer was extracted with ether (2
x 20 mL). The combined organic layerswere washed with saturated NaHC03
aqueous solution (15 mL), brine (15 mL), and driedover MgS04. Solvents
were removed under vacuum to give the crude residue, which waspurified by
silica flash chromatography (10% to 30% ethyl acetate in hexanes) to give
yield 0.80 g, 89%. 1H NMR (CDC13, 400 MHz) δ 7.42 -7.38 (m, 2H),
7.36-7.27 (m, 3H), 6.82 (d, J = 16.0Hz, lH), 6.18 (dd, J = 6.56, 16.0 Hz,
lH), 4.64 (m, lH), 2.32 (brs, 1H)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Heterocyclic Carbene Catalyzed Trifluoromethylation of Carbonyl
Compounds
