$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To aldehyde (0.63 g, 5.6 mmol) in a dry flask under N2 were added DMF
(anhydrous, 5 mL) and MSCF3 (2.4 g, 16.8 mmol). After the mixture was
cooled to -25 °C, carbene (9 mg,0.028 mmol, 0.005 eq) was added. The
mixture was warmed to room temperature and stirred at that temperature
for 1 h. A 2 N HC1 solution (6 mL) was added and the solutionwas stirred
at room temperature until all TMS protected intermediate converted
toproduct. Water (30 mL) was added and the aqueous layer was extracted
with ether (2x20 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with
saturated NaHC03 aqueous solution (15 mL), brine (15 mL), and dried over
MgS04. Solvents were removed undervacuum to give the crude residue, which
was purified by silica flash chromatography(10% to 30% ethyl acetate in
hexanes) to give yield 0.83 g,81%. 1H NMR (CDC13,400 MHz) δ 3.72 (m, lH),
2.05 (d, J = 6.64 Hz, lH), 1.91 (d, J = 12.04Hz, lH), 1.84-1.63 (m, 5H),
1.33-1.10 (m, 5H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Heterocyclic Carbene Catalyzed Trifluoromethylation of Carbonyl
Compounds
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Song, Jinhua J.; Tan, Zhulin; Reeves, Jonathan T.; Gallou, Fabrice; Yee,
Nathan K.; Senanayake, Chris H.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2005), 7(11), 2193-2196

