$DATUM 1,1,1-Trifluoro-6-[(1-phenyl-1H-tetrazol-5-yl)thio]hexan-2-ol (19)
Trimethyl(trifluoromethyl)silane (625 μL, 4.23 mmol) was added to a
solution of freshly prepared aldehyde 18 (925 mg, 3.53 mmol) in THF (18
mL) and the mixture was cooled to 0°C. Then TBAF (1 M in THF, 353 μL,
0.35 mmol) was added dropwise, and the mixture was allowed to warm to
room temperature. After1 h, 1 N HCl (18 mL) was added and the mixture was
stirred for another hour, when TLC monitoring showed complete conversion
[petroleum ether/ethyl acetate (1:1); UV]. Water (30 mL) and Et2O (30 mL)
were added, the aqueous layer was separated and extracted with Et2O (3 x
30 mL). The combined organic layers were dried over Na2SO4, filtered and
the solvent was removed in vacuo. The crude product was subjected to
flash chromatography on silica gel [petroleum ether/ethyl acetate (3/1)].
19 (1.02 g, 3.07 mmol, 87%) as colorless oil. Rf (19) = 0.45, 1H NMR
(300.13 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 1.51-1.81 (m, 4 H, 3-H, 4-H), 1.82-1.99 (m, 2 H,
5-H), 3.27 (bs, 1 H, OH), 3.38 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 2 H, 6-H), 3.86-4.08 (m, 1
H, 2-H), 7.46-7.65 (m, 5 H, Ph) ppm. 13C NMR (75.48 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
24.09, 29.00 (2t, C-3, C-4), 28.87 (t, C-5), 33.01 (t, C-6), 70.14 (q,
JC,F = 31.0 Hz, C-2), 123.99, 129.93, 130.34 (3d, CH-Ph), 125.29 (q, JC,F
= 282.0 Hz, C-1), 133.68 (s, C-Ph), 153.56 (s, C-tetrazole) ppm. HR-MS
(ESI+): m/z calcd. for C13H15F3N4OSNa+ 355.0816 [M+Na]+; found 355.0810.
