$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure A: Aryl Trifluoroethanol
Synthesis. To a solution of the desired aldehyde (1 equiv) in DMF (0.3 M)
in a round-bottom flask under argon were successively added
trimethyl(trifluoromethyl)silane (2 equiv) and potassium carbonate (5 mol
%). The reaction mixture was stirred at rt over 4-16 h (monitor by TLC),
then 2N HCl was added and the solution further was stirred over 4-16 h
(monitor by TLC). Water was added and the crude product was extracted
with EtOAc, washed with water, brine, dried with MgSO4, concentrated
under reduced pressure, and purified by silica gel chromatography.
1-(4-Fluoro-3-methoxyphenyl)-2,2,2-trifluoroethanol 8k. Prepared
according to general procedure A from the corresponding aldehyde (3.00 g,
19.5 mmol), purified by silica gel chromatography (petroleum ether/EtOAc
80:20) and obtained as a colorless oil in 87% yield (3.72 g). 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.11 (dd, J = 8.0 Hz, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.09 (dd, J = 10.8 Hz,
8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.02-6.95 (m, 1H), 4.98 (m, 1H), 3.90 (s, 3H), 3.04 (d, J =
4.5 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 153.0 (d, J = 248.2 Hz), 147.7
(d, J = 11.0 Hz), 130.21, 124.07 (q, J = 282.6 Hz), 120.2 (d, J = 7.3
Hz), 116.0 (d, J = 18.8 Hz), 112.4, 72.2 (q, J = 32.2 Hz), 56.3. 19F NMR
(377 MHz, CDCl3) δ -78.5 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 3F),-133.8 (m, 1F). HRMS (FI)
Calc'd for C9H8F4O2 (M) 223.0460, Found 223.0456.
