$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To 4-Methoxybenzaldehyde (0.61 mL, 5.0 mmol) in a dry flask under N2 were
addedDMF (anhydrous, 5 mL), TMSCF3 (2.1 g, 15 mmol), and carbene 1 (17
mg, 0.05 mmol).The mixture was stirred at room temperature until aldehyde
was consumed as determinedby HPLC (2 h 10 min). HCl solution (2 N, 6 mL)
was added and the solution was stirredat room temperature until all TMS
protected intermediate converted to product. Water(30 mL) was added and
the aqueous layer was extracted with ether (20 mLx2). Organiclayers were
combined and washed with saturated NaHC03 aqueous solution (15 mL),brine
(15 mL), dried over MgS04. Solvents were removed under vacuum to give
thecrude residue, which was purified by silica flash chromatography (30%
MTBEJhexanes)to give yield 0.835g, 81%. 1H NMR (CDC13, 400 MHz) δ 7.38
(d, J = 8.68 Hz, 2H), 6.92 (d, J = 8.80 Hz, 2H), 4.95 (m, lH), 3.81 (s,
3H), 2.67 (d, J = 4.48 Hz, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Heterocyclic Carbene Catalyzed Trifluoromethylation of Carbonyl
Compounds
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
