$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To aldehyde (0.68 g, 4.8 mmol) in a dry flask under Nt were added DMF
(anhydrous, 5 mL)and TMSCF3 (1.9 g, 13.5 mmol). AEter the mixture was
cooled to -25 O C , carbene 1 (8mg, 0.024 mmol, 0.005 eq) was added. The
mixture was warmed to room temperatureand stirred at that temperature
until 5c was consumed as determined by HPLC (60 min). A 2 N HCl solution
(6 mL) was added and the solution was stirred at room temperatureuntil
all TMS protected intermediate converted to product. Water (30 mL) was
added and the aqueous layer was extracted with ether (2 x 20 mL). The
combined organic layerswere washed with saturated NaHC03 aqueous solution
(15 mL), brine (15 mL), and driedover MgS04. Solvents were removed under
vacuum to give the crude residue, which waspurified by silica flash
chromatography (10% to 30% ethyl acetate in hexanes) to give yield 0.88
g, 86%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 7.49-7.38 (m, 4H), 5.04 (m, lH), 2.65
(d, J = 3.28 Hz, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Heterocyclic Carbene Catalyzed Trifluoromethylation of Carbonyl
Compounds
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
