$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the addition of TMSCF3
to the α-amino N-tert-butylsulfinimines: Into a round-bottomed
flame-dried 25 mL flask containing 5 mL THF, fitted with a magnetic
stirring bar, rubber septum and an argon-filled balloon were placed 0.5
mmol of imine and 1.2 equiv. of TMAF (tetramethylammonium fluoride). The
resulting solution was cooled to -35°C and a solution of 1.5 equiv. of
TMSCF3 in 5 mL THF was added slowly via syringe. The reaction mixture was
stirred at -35°C until the reaction was complete (usually 1-2h). The
reaction mixture was warmed to -10°C and quenched with 2 mL saturated
NH4Cl, extracted with ethyl acetate, dried over Na2SO4 and evaporated to
give the crude product. Amine derivatives (3a-g) were purified with the
recourse of flash chromatography using ethyl acetate and hexanes.
Compound 3b, Yield 85%. [α]20D -85.3 (c 1.0, CHCl3). 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 0.77(3H, t, J= 6.91 Hz), 1.23 (9H, s), 1.28- 1.41 (2H, m),
1.50-1.62 (2H, m), 3.19 (1H, m), 3.60 (2H, d, J= 13.5 Hz), 3.82 (2H, d,
J= 13.8 Hz), 3.97 (1H, d, J= 7.4 Hz), 4.07 (1H, m), 7.21- 7.33 (10H, m):
13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ 13.7, 19.9, 22.4, 28.9, 54.0, 56.6 (q,2JC-F=
28.4 Hz), 56.9, 57.7, 125.7 (q,1JC-F= 281 Hz), 127.0, 128.2, 129.0,
138.9: 19F NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ = -73.2 (d, JF- H = 7.46 Hz).
HRMS(DCI/NH3) m/z calced for C24H34F3N2OS (M+H+) 455.2344, found
455.2327.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
