$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To p-acetyl benzaldehyde (5n, 0.296 g, 2.0 mmol) in a dry flask under N2
were addedDMF (anhydrous, 6 mL), TMSCF3 (1.5 mL, 10 mmol). Carbene (3.4
mg, 0.01 mmol)was added. The mixture was stirred at room temperature for
30 min. NaOH aqueoussolution (6 N, 3 mL) was added and the solution was
stirred at room temperature until allTMS protected intermediate converted
to product. The mixture was neutralized to pH 7using HC1 aqueous solution
(6 N). The aqueous layer was extracted with MTBE (20mLx2). Organic layers
were combined and dried over MgS04. Solvents were removedunder vacuum to
give the crude residue, which was purified by flash chromatography(10%
ethyl acetatelhexanes) to give yield 0.37 g, 85%. 1 H NMR (CDC13, 400
MHz) 6 8.00 (d, J = 6.80 Hz, 2H), 7.60 (d, J = 8.08 Hz, 2H), 5.12 (m,
lH), 2.71 (d, J = 4.56 Hz, lH), 2.63 (s, 3H). 13c NMR (CDC13, 100 MHz) 6
198.3, 139.1, 137.7, 128.5, 128.2, 127.4, 126.4, 124.0 (q, JC-F = 281Hz),
72.2 (q, JC-F = 32 HZ),26.7. HRMS (APCI positive): calc'd for [M+1]+
C10H1002F3, m/z 219.0627, obs'd m/z219.0630.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Heterocyclic Carbene Catalyzed Trifluoromethylation of Carbonyl
Compounds
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
