$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a DMF (anhydrous, 3.0 mL) solution of aldehyde (0.150 g, 1.0 mmol)
were added TMSCF3(0.74 mL, 5 mmol) and carbene (3.4 mg, 0.01 mmol). The
mixture was stirred at roomtemperature for 30 rnin. A 2 N HC1 solution (6
mL) was added and the solution wasstirred at room temperature until all
TMS protected intermediate converted to product.Water (30 mL) was added
and the aqueous layer was extracted with dichloromethane (20mL x 5).
Solvents were removed under vacuum to give yield 185 mg, 84%. 1 H NMR
(MeOH-d4, 400 MHz) δ 7.93 (d, J = 8.32 Hz, 2H), 7.49 (d, J = 8.08 Hz,
2H), 5.01 (q, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Heterocyclic Carbene Catalyzed Trifluoromethylation of Carbonyl
Compounds
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
