$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical procedure for the trifluoromethylation of aminoketones is as
follows: Trimethyl(trifluoromethyl)silane (TMS-CF3) (0.5 mmol) was added
to a solution of 4-(diethylamino)-2-butanone (1, 0.6 mmol) in dry DMF
(1.0 ml) and the mixture was stirred at room temperature for 3 h under an
Ar atmosphere.
4-(diethylamino)-1,1,1-trifluoro-2-methyl-2-(trimethylsilyloxy)-butane,
yield 82%. 1H-NMR (TMS, CDCl3): δ = 0.16 (s, 9H), 1.04 (t, J = 7.2 Hz,
6H), 1.37 (d, J = 0.5 Hz, 3H), 1.6-2.0 (bm, 4H), 2.52 (q, J = 7.2 Hz,
4H); 19F-NMR (CFCI3, CDCl3): δ = -82.41 (s).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Unique reactivity of amino ketones in the trifluoromethylation with
trialkyl(trifluoromethyl)silanes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
