$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To hydrocinnamaldehyde (5h, 0.66 mL, 5.0 mmol) in a dry flask under N2
were added DMF (anhydrous, 5 mL), TMSCF3 (2.1 g, 15 mmol), and carbene
(17 mg, 0.05 mmol).The mixture was stirred at room temperature until
aldehyde was consumed as determinedby HPLC (3 h). HC1 solution (2 N, 6
mL) was added and the solution was stirred at room temperature until all
TMS protected intermediate converted to product. Water (30 mL) was added
and the aqueous layer was extracted with ether (20 mLx2). Organic
layerswere combined and washed with saturated NaHC03 aqueous solution (15
mL), brine (15mL), dried over MgS04. Solvents were removed under vacuum
to give the crude residue,which was purified by silica flash
chromatography (20% Et20/hexanes) to give yield 0.816 g, 80%. 1H NMR
(CDC13, 400 MHz) δ 7.30 (m, 2H), 7.22 (m, 3H), 3.88 (m, lH), 2.92 (m,
lH), 2.74 (m, lH), 2.22 (d, J = 6.12 Hz, lH), 2.05-1.85 (m, 2H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Heterocyclic Carbene Catalyzed Trifluoromethylation of Carbonyl
Compounds
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
