$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure for the trifluoromethylation
of aminoketones is as follows: Trimethyl(trifluoromethyl)silane (TMS-CF3)
(0.5 mmol) was added to a solution of 4-(diethylamino)-2-butanone (1, 0.6
mmol) in dry DMF (1.0 ml) and the mixture was stirred at room temperature
for 3 h under an Ar atmosphere.
5-(diethylamino)-1,1,1-trifluoro-2-methyl-2-(trimethylsilyloxy)-pentane,
yield 78%. 1H-NMR (TMS, CDCl3): δ = 0.15 (s, 9H), 1.02 (t, J = 7.2 Hz,
6H), 1.36 (d, J = 0.6 Hz, 3H), 1.5-1.8 (bm, 4H), 2.37- 2.45 (m, 2H), 2.53
(q, J = 7.2 Hz, 4H); 19F-NMR (CFCI3, CDCl3): δ = - 82.32 (s).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Unique reactivity of amino ketones in the trifluoromethylation with
trialkyl(trifluoromethyl)silanes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Hagiwara, Toshiki; Mochizuki, Hiroaki; Fuchikami, Takamasa
